  {
    "number": 59,
    "title": "docs: plan PC and desk lighting integrations and backlog",
    "body": "PC and desk lighting lacked a documented integration path and implementation backlog. Add a controller guide, architecture and roadmap links for Corsair RAM and supported H150i lighting, optional Lian Li Strimer, and the Varmilo VA108M-RGB keyboard. Preserve iCUE, L-Connect 3 and normal keyboard behavior, with one writer per lighting target.\n\nVarmilo starts with whole-keyboard shared agent status through an existing supported interface. If none qualifies, its integration stays deferred. Per-key displays, custom protocol research, simulated keypress control and firmware replacement are excluded. Keyboard support does not block Corsair or Strimer delivery; Strimer does not block Corsair.\n\nRefs #50. The eleven future skeletons #51-#58 and #60-#62 remain open for refinement before implementation. The existing guide #35 links them. Keyboard participation in shared status #55 and controls #56 conditionally requires #61, without making either shared issue depend on keyboard delivery.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Node 24.20.0: `npm run check:workflow` and `npm run test:workflow` passed, including all 10 tests. Dependencies were installed with `npm ci` for the preceding documentation candidate; manifests and lockfile are unchanged.\n- Checked 25 local Markdown links and `git diff --check`.\n- Read back the updated issues and verified every native prerequisite relationship in their transitive graph in both directions: 29 issues, 52 edges, no cycles. Seven edges belong to the three new keyboard issues.\n- Existing OpenSpec inventory: two capabilities, zero active changes and two archived changes, all applicable validation passed. This change has no product behavior or contract delta, so it introduces no OpenSpec change, runtime package, service or installation.\n\n## Review comparison\n\nBase and merge-base: `a7b1aa0476c2f3e0561b5d53dbc8395353180d60`.\nCandidate head: `baf2b0bc2eb2b7839afe98175d8f3c686e5860c4`.\nDiff: `git diff a7b1aa0476c2f3e0561b5d53dbc8395353180d60...baf2b0bc2eb2b7839afe98175d8f3c686e5860c4`.\n\nIndependent read-only Standards and Specification reviews both found no issues against this exact comparison. The worktree is clean. Standards review checked repository rules, ownership, contract and evidence boundaries, and the linked vendor/OpenRGB claims. Specification review reconciled both eleven-row documentation dependency tables against the issue graph and accepted scope.\n\n## CI and device evidence\n\nGitHub refused to start all eight jobs in each current-head workflow: [PR run](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/actions/runs/34176141304) and [branch run](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/actions/runs/34176139337). All sixteen jobs have zero executed steps. Annotations report failed account payments or a spending limit requiring an increase. This is an account execution blocker, not a failed test assertion.\n\nMerge remains blocked by `AGENTS.md` and `docs/sdlc.md`. Resolve the GitHub billing/spending restriction, rerun both workflows, and refresh current base/head/reviews. Merge only after every configured job succeeds, using the guarded squash procedure. Verify all merged-revision main CI jobs before closing #50. No merge or account-setting change was performed.\n\nHardware evidence is limited to user-supplied model information, application screenshots, historical records and read-only generic Windows inventory. Keyboard automation compatibility remains unverified. Source, installation, real-client, transport, visible-light and typing/restoration evidence remain separate. This PR does not operate hardware or alter installed software.\n",
    "state": "open",
